{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented RED-first per the plan.\n\nRED (against the tree, before the fix), 3 new tests failing:\n- test_pass1_ladder_retry_stays_on_the_run_s_own_bedrock_model:\n  observed retry models ['claude-opus-4-8', 'claude-opus-4-8'] !=\n  ['bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8-v1:0', ...]\n- test_models_at_or_above_keeps_a_bedrock_primary_on_bedrock_with_no_classes:\n  ['claude-opus-4-8'] != ['bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8-v1:0']\n- test_models_at_or_above_drops_unnameable_higher_rungs:\n  ['claude-haiku-4-5','claude-sonnet-4-6','claude-opus-4-8'] !=\n  ['bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-v1:0']\n\nThe two guard tests (the _too_big failure-path case and the out-of-scope start-rung\npin for a non-Anthropic FAMILY primary) were green before and after, as intended.\n\nFix: _rung_target now takes the run's primary model plus an own_rung flag and returns\nstr | None. It resolves the rung through its class exactly as before, then compares\ninfer_provider(primary) with infer_provider(target): agree or either undeterminable ->\ntoday's value byte-for-byte; differ on the primary's own rung -> the primary verbatim;\ndiffer on a higher rung -> None, dropped. models_at_or_above threads the primary on the\nlocated-start-rung branch only and filters the Nones; the no-match fallback is unchanged.\n\nMODEL_LADDER and largest_window_tokens are untouched, so escalation WINDOWS stay keyed on\nconcrete families while escalation TARGETS move to the class vocabulary.\n\nEvery pre-existing test is unmodified: git diff on tests/ is 93 insertions, 0 deletions.\nmake lint exit 0, make typecheck exit 0 (mypy clean, 411 files)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785644882656029001,"uuid":"1ecd72e8-0906-473c-bc43-011cad72f9cb"}